What is Petroleum Coke?
Petroleum coke is the carbon‑rich by‑product of the oil‑refining coking process. Its high calorific value (typically 7,800–8,200 kcal/kg) and low ash content make it a premium fuel for high‑temperature industrial processes. Different grades-needle, sponge, shot and honeycomb-are tailored to meet the performance requirements of power generation, cement production, aluminum smelting, steelmaking, and increasingly, specialty applications such as battery‑grade graphite production.

